#: assets/js/chat-ui.js:2417
#, js-format
msgid ""
"1. Claim API credits from an eligible subscription by linking an API organization, or add paid API credit. See [OpenAI eligibility and activation](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/chatgpt-api-credits) or [Claude eligibility and activation](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/api-credits-for-subscribers).\n"
"2. Create an API key in that organization on the [OpenAI API platform](https://platform.openai.com/api-keys) or [Claude Console](https://platform.claude.com/settings/keys).\n"
"3. Add the key for the matching provider in [%1$s](%2$s), then choose a model in AI Assistant.\n"
"\n"
"Requests use your provider’s API balance."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/chat-ui.js:2418
msgid ""
"**A privacy-friendly, free alternative.** Run AI on your own device without sending your prompts to a cloud AI provider.\n"
"\n"
"1. Install [Ollama](https://ollama.com/) or [LM Studio](https://lmstudio.ai/) on this device, download a model, and start the local server. Allow requests from this website in the server’s browser access / CORS settings."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/chat-ui.js:2420
#, js-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"2. Open [AI Assistant settings](%s) and click **Scan again** next to **Save Changes**. LM Studio (localhost:1234) and Ollama (localhost:11434) are detected directly from this browser; no WordPress provider plugin is required."
